module_signature: |
  module seq_detector_0011(
      input clk,
      input reset,
      input data_in,
      output reg detected
  );
sequence_to_detect: '0011'
sample_input: '0001100110110010'
sample_output: '0000010001000000'
timing: |
  detected is a Moore output: it depends only on the FSM state, never directly on data_in.
  It is high during the ONE clock cycle that follows the rising edge which samples the last '1'
  of "0011". Overlapping sequences are detected (e.g. "0011" after "0011" -> detected twice).
  How sample_input / sample_output line up: sample_output[i] is the value of detected while
  sample_input[i] is applied (it reflects only the bits sampled BEFORE sample_input[i]).
  Race-free testbench: hold reset high for 2 rising edges, release it on a falling edge, then
  on EVERY falling edge i: first check detected == sample_output[i], then drive
  data_in = sample_input[i]. Never check exactly at a rising edge or a few ps after it.


